  "notes_for_editor": "Newspaper search (Chronicling America) timed out, so no keeper-level newspaper material. Keeper roster is the USLHS archive's, unverified against primary registers; it shows overlapping first assistants in 1936-37 (Donelly, Scriver) and LighthouseFriends also names Nicholas Kashevaroff as head in 1941, which USLHS lists only as first assistant. 1941-1959 has almost no roster entries. The 1925 Bulletin gives commissioning as 20 November while UAA and LighthouseFriends give 11 December; the story states the disagreement. Wartime history, the 1985 helicopter episode and the USCG Historian page (blocked) were not used. LighthouseFriends anecdotes (Reager, O'Brien, Newberry) are second-hand recollections, paraphrased. Wrecks list empty: no source tying a wreck to the station was found. Commissioner report page numbers (83, 66) from corpus.py page; 1922 page 66 matched by the earlier grep snippet only. Facts.light first_lit 1913 is the unwatched lantern; the manned 1925 light is Fl W 10s per Bulletin. Bulletin 1925 p.47 is two-column and the OCR interleaves the columns, so those sentences were reassembled from the interleaved lines and should be checked against the page image.",
